    "scienceEn": "Ordinary cheeses (Gouda, Cheddar, Mozzarella) are made from CASEIN proteins coagulated by rennet. The remaining green liquid is 'whey' (Molke). Ricotta ('re-cooked') is made by heating this leftover whey to 85-90°C with an acidifier: heat denatures the dissolved ALBUMIN and GLOBULIN whey proteins, causing them to float to the top as delicate sweet curds!\\nNorwegian Brunost boils whey for hours until lactose caramelizes into brown fudge.",
