    "scienceEn": "Olive varieties express dramatically different fatty acid and polyphenol profiles: 1) Koroneiki (Greece): Tiny drought-hardy fruit with over 75% oleic acid and herbaceous aromas of wild thyme and green pepper. 2) Picual (Spain / Jaén): World's most planted variety; massive polyphenol content (up to 800+ mg/kg) gives intense stability and natural bitterness, making it the most heat-resistant olive oil. 3) Arbequina (Spain): Low in bitter polyphenols, creamy, ripe with aromas of green almond and apple—ideal for desserts or guests sensitive to bitterness.",
